   "subject": "Adding a number of lines to a boxplot / sorting (again)",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\">Hi!<br><br>I want to boxplot vectors in a list, ordered them by median and add vertical(horizontal) lines to the plot:<br><br>list1 &lt;- lapply(dir(), read.table,  sep = &quot;\\t&quot;, dec = &quot;.&quot;)<br>names(list1) &lt;- gsub(&quot;.tsv&quot;, &quot;&quot;, c(dir()))<br>vector1 &lt;- lapply(list1, function(x) {as.numeric(as.vector(unlist(x)))})<br>med &lt;- sapply(vector1, median)<br><br>old.par &lt;- par(no.readonly=TRUE)<br>par(las=2)<br>boxplot(vector1[order(med, decreasing=TRUE)])<br>abline(h=87.65, col=&quot;Red&quot;)<br>abline(h=83.55, col=&quot;Green&quot;)<br>abline(h=80.38, col=&quot;Blue&quot;)<br><br>The resulting plot looks as depicted in the bottom (first pic).<br><br>I want to do it in ggplot, mainly because i want to have a legend for the horizontal lines. I started with a melt:<br><br>v1m  &lt;- melt(vector1)<br><br>and then do<br><br>ggplot(data=v1m, aes(x=L1, y=value)) +<br>  stat_boxplot(geom =&#39;errorbar&#39;) + <br>  geom_boxplot()+<br>  theme_bw() +<br>  coord_flip()<br><br><b>The\r\n first question is: How to put the ordering by median in to action?</b> I \r\nknow this has been asked ad nauseam on the web, but there are always \r\nlittle twists to each individual problems.<br><br>Then its about adding those lines. I added: <br>geom_hline(aes(yintercept=87.8), colour=&quot;red&quot;, linetype = &quot;longdash&quot;) +, <br>, which was fine, but as the intercept are coming from a dataframe:</p><p style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\"><span style=\"border-collapse:separate;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:14px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:13px;text-align:-webkit-left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:pre-wrap;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(225,226,229)\"></span></p><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:10pt!important;outline-style:none;outline-width:initial;outline-color:initial;border-top-style:none;border-right-style:none;border-bottom-style:none;border-left-style:none;border-width:initial;border-color:initial;white-space:pre-wrap!important;word-break:break-all;margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;line-height:1.2\"><font size=\"2\"><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\">      ID Value\r\n1  treat1 94.80\r\n2  treat2 87.65\r\n3  treat3 83.55\r\n4  treat4 80.38\r\n5  treat5 77.43<br><br>I wanted to add it as a whole, in order to get a legend out of it:<br><br></span></font><br><font size=\"2\"><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\"><span style=\"border-collapse:separate;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:14px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:13px;text-align:-webkit-left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:pre-wrap;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(225,226,229)\"><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:10pt!important;outline-style:none;outline-width:initial;outline-color:initial;border-top-style:none;border-right-style:none;border-bottom-style:none;border-left-style:none;border-width:initial;border-color:initial;white-space:pre-wrap!important;word-break:break-all;margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;line-height:1.2\"><font size=\"2\"><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\"><span style=\"border-collapse:separate;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:13px;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:pre-wrap;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(225,226,229)\"><pre style=\"outline-style:none;outline-width:initial;outline-color:initial;border-style:none;border-width:initial;border-color:initial;white-space:pre-wrap!important;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;line-height:1.2\"><span>geom_line(data=df, aes(x=Value, y=ID, colour=ID)) +<br><br>but got<br><br></span></pre></span></span></font></pre></span></span><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\"><span style=\"border-collapse:separate;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:13px;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:pre-wrap;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(225,226,229)\"><pre style=\"outline-style:none;outline-width:initial;outline-color:initial;border-style:none;border-width:initial;border-color:initial;white-space:pre-wrap!important;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;line-height:1.2\"><span style=\"border-collapse:separate;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:14px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:13px;text-align:-webkit-left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:pre-wrap;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(225,226,229)\"><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:10pt!important;outline-style:none;outline-width:initial;outline-color:initial;border-top-style:none;border-right-style:none;border-bottom-style:none;border-left-style:none;border-width:initial;border-color:initial;white-space:pre-wrap!important;word-break:break-all;margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;line-height:1.2\"><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">geom_path: Each group consist of only one observation. Do you need to adjust the group aesthetic?</span></pre></span></pre></span><br><span style=\"border-collapse:separate;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:13px;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:pre-wrap;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(225,226,229)\"></span></span></font><font size=\"2\"><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\"><br><b>The second question: Any idea how to solve this?</b></span></font><br></pre><p></p><p style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\">Thank you very much!<br></p><p style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\"><br></p><p style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\"><br></p><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" href=\"https://lh4.googleusercontent.com/--2HsCaa8Eio/VIa1bxaiZRI/AAAAAAAAAAk/rQX_PiIKZaQ/s1600/Capture.JPG\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh4.googleusercontent.com/--2HsCaa8Eio/VIa1bxaiZRI/AAAAAAAAAAk/rQX_PiIKZaQ/s1600/Capture.JPG&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792369828880000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2OazOBSgZbfWPNPl1QRI2T\"><img src=\"https://lh4.googleusercontent.com/--2HsCaa8Eio/VIa1bxaiZRI/AAAAAAAAAAk/rQX_PiIKZaQ/s320/Capture.JPG\" height=\"207\" width=\"320\" border=\"0\"></a></p><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><br></p><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"></p><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><br></p><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><br></p><br><br><br><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><br></p></div>"
    ]
